[-1.20000005,2,1.5]", "Prior to the documentation edit, library files totaled 13318 bytes and Python had 118 lines; the small edit leaves the library well within the specified limits."],\n  "selection_probe": "Editable and deliberately incomplete synthetic room-inspired probe at /app/selection_probe.blend, rendered at /app/selection_probe.png, generated by /app/validation_probe.py. It includes a table, leg, floor, wall, door, jamb and handle; it is not a reconstruction or image-plane copy. Incorrect parent assignment changed handle and leg world positions, invalidating intended assembly and support relationships; the render was not visually compared with the reference. Selection GT was not accessed.",\n  "failed_or_rejected_candidates": ["Probe assembly candidate rejected as a structurally valid door/table test: direct parent assignment caused child transforms to jump. The hinge pivot test alone passed. The bar AABB candidate was not confirmed as an intersection. No non-executable library unit was identified."],\n  "changes": ["Updated /app/library/SKILL.md to warn that parenting requires preserving child world matrices and checking positions. Retained callable code without modification."],\n  "remaining_unvalidated_methods": ["Image-similarity improvement, reference-specific camera or layout recovery and occlusion accuracy", "Correctly parented complete hinge assembly, wall clearance and opening preservation", "Visual grain direction, control-render effect, appearance similarity, and image-texture resources", "Confirmed surface contact, physical support, and mesh intersection", "Transfer to independent scenes and final test"],\n  "applicability_and_side_effects": "Camera aiming mutates camera transforms; hinge_pose mutates its supplied root and does not cut openings or check collision. Parent assignment can change child world transforms. Material creation adds a datablock and requires explicit binding; procedural noise uses object-local coordinates. Support bounds 